{"rule": "Return this JSON object with the rule field unchanged and a new passage of about 250 words in the text field.", "text": "By October the wigwam had come down. Her mother pulled the canes from the soil one at a time and stacked them in the shed, and the girl gathered the last dry pods from the ground where the frost had loosened them. She laid the beans out on newspaper along the windowsill in the back bedroom, where the sun came in low and pale in the afternoons, and turned them every day with the flat of her hand. When they rattled in her palm she knew they were ready. She chose carefully. The biggest and the most evenly speckled went into a jam jar for the garden. A handful of the rest went into a twist of paper, and on the paper she wrote the name her grandmother had always used, which was not the name on any packet. Then she opened the notebook to a clean page and drew the tin of seeds from Aberdeen, each twist labelled as her cousin had labelled them. Beside the one she could not read she drew a question mark and underlined it twice. She decided she would plant that one first, in spring, and find out what it was by watching. Her mother found brown paper in the drawer and a length of garden twine. The girl added a letter, longer than her cousin's, about the yellow leaves and the frost and the rattle of the beans when they were dry. At the bottom she asked what the sea sounded like in winter. Then she tied the parcel up and carried it to the post office herself."}
